From e85ba9e808c5ade74dc4181a0a50602d07d470f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rustdesk-cortendesk-pve release <rustdesk-cortendesk-pve release>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:16:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] websocket: WebSocket builds get wss://, the site's
 WebSocket name and their relay

A client with allow-websocket=Y (an option under Other) reaches hbbs and
hbbr as wss://<Host>/ws/id and /ws/relay. On a site whose ID server name
forwards only the raw ports while the console (behind a tunnel, say)
bridges /ws/id and /ws/relay, such a build needs the console's name as
Host: with the pre-filled raw name it got the console's HTML page instead
of a WebSocket and never registered, although the console showed it
online through the API heartbeat. A normal client can't use the console's
name either, and a WebSocket client and a normal one can't connect.

The client also picks wss:// only when its api-server OPTION starts with
https (hbb_common check_ws; the API server built into the client does not
count), and rdgen sets that option only for Incoming Only builds. Other
WebSocket builds used ws://<Host>/ws/id, a tunnel answered with a redirect
to https the client can't follow, and they never registered either.

For every build whose effective allow-websocket is Y (override-settings
first, then default-settings, as RustDesk reads them): with an https://
API server it gets api-server=<it> in the map that turns WebSocket on,
unless it sets one (Incoming Only already has it in override-settings);
with another API server it is refused when its Host is a public name (not
an IP address, reached as ws://<ip>:21118, nor a LAN-only name).

RDGEN_DEFAULT_WS_SERVER names the WebSocket host. When it is set, valid
and not the same name as RDGEN_DEFAULT_SERVER, a WebSocket build
- gets the WebSocket name for an empty Host (form and /api/generate);
- is refused with the raw name as Host, relay-server or
  custom-rendezvous-server, with a message on that field;
- gets relay-server=<Host> in the map that turns WebSocket on unless it
  sets a relay-server itself, because a client's own relay-server wins
  over the relay hbbs names, which is the raw name.
Any other build is refused with the WebSocket name. The form explains the
two names under Host. Unset, invalid or the same name: these name rules
are off.

api-server and relay-server live in the custom settings, inside the base64
custom value, so the runner's validate.py sees no new key. Tests for each
rule, the dispatched configs against validate.py, and SETUP-PULL.md and
rdgen.env.example describe the setting.
