index 2476c01..5054c48 100644
--- a/SETUP-PULL.md
+++ b/SETUP-PULL.md
@@ -136,6 +136,8 @@ Notes:
   - `GHBRANCH`: the branch `init` pushed to, which is the repository's default branch (`init` prints it)
   - `GHBEARER`: the runtime token
 - Optional defaults: `RDGEN_DEFAULT_SERVER`, `RDGEN_DEFAULT_PORT`, `RDGEN_DEFAULT_API_SERVER` and `RDGEN_DEFAULT_KEY_FILE` (the hbbs `id_ed25519.pub` in the same LXC) prefill the form, as do `RDGEN_DEFAULT_URL_LINK`, `RDGEN_DEFAULT_DOWNLOAD_LINK` and `RDGEN_DEFAULT_COMPANY`. Installed Windows clients download the update URL and run it, so it has to be a direct link to an installer. With `RDGEN_UPDATE_BASE` set, the form suggests `<base>/<windows-x86_64|windows-x86>/<version>/<name>.exe` for Windows builds of a 1.4.x version; the RustDesk LXC answers it with the newest published build of that name with a newer version, or 404.
+- `RDGEN_DEFAULT_WS_SERVER`: when WebSocket clients (`allow-websocket=Y` under Other) reach the server through another name than `RDGEN_DEFAULT_SERVER`, such as a console behind a tunnel that bridges only `/ws/id` and `/ws/relay`. A WebSocket build then gets that name for an empty Host and is refused with `RDGEN_DEFAULT_SERVER` as Host (or as `relay-server`/`custom-rendezvous-server`); a normal build is refused with the WebSocket name. A WebSocket build without its own `relay-server` gets `relay-server=<Host>` in the settings map that turns WebSocket on, because the client's own option wins over the relay hbbs names. Unset, invalid or the same name: these name rules are off.
+- WebSocket builds and the API server: the client picks `wss://` only when its `api-server` option starts with `https` (the API server built into the client does not count), and rdgen sets that option itself only for Incoming Only builds. So every WebSocket build whose API server is `https://` gets `api-server=<it>` in the settings map that turns WebSocket on, unless it sets one; one whose API server is not `https://` is refused when its Host is a public name, since `ws://` through a tunnel or an https-only proxy gets a redirect the client cannot follow. IP addresses (`ws://<ip>:21118`) and LAN-only names are left alone.
 - To serve rdgen under a sub-path instead of a port, set `RDGEN_URL_PREFIX=/rdgen` and include `deploy/nginx/rdgen-subpath.conf` in an existing server block. Keep its allow/deny list if that server block is reachable from the internet.
 - Memory, measured on Alpine: gunicorn master about 18 MB, worker about 57 MB, poller about 57 MB. Add about 2 MB for nginx.
 - Disk: a Windows build (exe + msi) is 50-60 MB. Builds are pruned after `RDGEN_RETENTION_DAYS` (default 30).
